		{
			dependencies: ["6A7BE998C2EC882D"]
			description: [
				"Right-clicking with a Wrench &9&lsets the output side of GT machines&r and &9&lconnects pipes&r, while sneak-right-clicking &9&lrotates machines&r and &9&llocks pipe flow&r (your offhand must be empty for this), and it can also break machines in place of a pickaxe"
				""
				"The Screwdriver &9&lopens the machine cover configuration screen&r and &9&ltoggles auto-output"
				""
				"The Wire Cutter &9&lconnects cables"
				""
				"Right-clicking with a Soft Mallet &9&lpauses a machine instantly&r, while sneak-right-clicking &9&lpauses it after the current recipe cycle finishes&r (unpausing can only be done with a normal right-click, not a sneak-right-click)"
				""
				"The Crowbar &9&lremoves covers"
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Wrench:"
				"When you hold a Wrench and aim at a block that accepts a wrench, a 3x3 grid is shown on each face of the block:"
				"The centre has the most, the edges come next, and the corners the least."
				"When you right-click the centre of a machine's face, the front is rotated to that face (for non-GT machines that only have face distinction) or the output is moved to that face (for GT machines); right-clicking an edge rotates the front to the face in that edge's direction; right-clicking a corner rotates the front to the face opposite the one you clicked. But if you right-click a non-GT machine with no face distinction, all of the above simply removes the machine. Shift-right-clicking the centre of a face rotates the front to that face (for all machines), and the rest is the same for edges and corners. For non-GT machines with no face distinction, all of the above also simply removes the machine."
				"Right-clicking the centre of a pipe's face changes nothing; right-clicking an edge connects/disconnects the pipe in that edge's direction; right-clicking a corner connects/disconnects the pipe in the opposite direction. Shift-right-clicking controls whether the corresponding face accepts input."
				"Right-clicking a non-front face of a log, hay bale, comparator, repeater, pumpkin, jack o'lantern, piston, sticky piston, dropper, dispenser, furnace, chest, trapped chest, ender chest or hopper rotates it;"
				"Right-clicking the front face of a crafting table, bookshelf, pumpkin, jack o'lantern, piston, sticky piston, dropper, dispenser, furnace, chest, trapped chest, ender chest or hopper removes it."
				"But besides these, blocks like levers and rails can still be rotated or removed."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Soft Mallet:"
				"Right-clicking turns a machine on/off."
				"Right-clicking a lit Redstone Lamp turns it off, and vice versa."
				"Right-clicking a Powered Rail activates it directly, and vice versa."
				"Right-clicking a log, hay bale, piston, sticky piston, dropper, dispenser, pumpkin, jack o'lantern, furnace, chest, trapped chest or hopper rotates the block;"
				""
				"Screwdriver:"
				"Used to adjust various output sides and crafting parts."
				"Right-clicking a machine's front or output side lets you toggle whether input from the output side is allowed."
				"Note: holding a Screwdriver while pointing at cables and pipes does show the 3x3 grid, but in practice it has no effect."
				"The correct explanation: if the face corresponding to the 3x3 grid can be controlled by the Screwdriver, this is the same as controlling that face directly; if it cannot, nothing happens. The rules are the same as for the Wrench."
				"Right-clicking a comparator or repeater rotates it."
				""
				"Crowbar:"
				"Used to pry up rails, pry open various crates, and remove covers."
			]
